{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"87eae90fb7cd26a5ddbf29f2e75d5bf43a69606e319c8baef047d6cee03704b9","digest":{"component_or_area":"infra/scripts/observability.sh metric publication","key_entities":["infra/scripts/observability.sh","aws cloudwatch put-metric-data","replication stream","voter stream","merge-change stream","deploy stream","autodeploy-marker streams","G2P stream","offset file","tests/scripts/test_observability_offsets_6a65.py","tests/scripts/test_observability_exit.py"],"problem_keywords":["cumulative counter","offset acknowledgement","CloudWatch","metric loss","transient failure","observability","put-metric-data"],"propositions":["Cumulative counter blocks in observability.sh persist their offset before CloudWatch accepts the datapoint, causing transient publish failures to permanently lose the interval's count.","When an aws cloudwatch put-metric-data call fails after the offset has already advanced, the next successful run computes zero from the already-incremented baseline instead of retrying the accumulated delta.","The same offset-before-publish defect affects seven metric streams across six code shapes: replication, voter, merge-change, deploy, both shared autodeploy-marker metrics, and G2P.","Offset should advance only after successful AWS publication; on failure the offset must remain byte-identical so the next run retries the accumulated delta."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787592610824499001,"uuid":"29479944-9684-43d8-bc43-7e2fdac4a829"}